      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <small>Last updated 8 October 2026</small>
      <h2>What slashkern is</h2>
      <p>slashkern is a free app where you try short practice projects in design, writing, code, video, selling online, music and prompting with AI, to see which ones you enjoy. The projects use made-up situations. Brand projects are samples for now, not a real offer from that brand.</p>
      <h2>Who can use it</h2>
      <p>slashkern is for people aged 18 or older. An account is optional.</p>
      <h2>What you write</h2>
      <p>What you write is yours. You allow slashkern to store it, and to sync or share it only in the ways described in the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> page. Do not write anything unlawful, and do not write other people's personal details.</p>
      <h2>Slash</h2>
      <p>Slash is an AI, not a person. It asks questions and can get things wrong. It does not give professional, medical, legal or financial advice, and it does not decide anything for you. If things feel heavy, talk to someone you trust or to your local emergency services.</p>
      <h2>Using slashkern fairly</h2>
      <p>Do not try to break the service, copy it in bulk or use it to bother other people. Tips you leave on a project are shown without your name, and we may remove one that breaks these terms.</p>
      <h2>No guarantees</h2>
      <p>slashkern is an early version, offered as it is. We work to keep it running, but we cannot promise it is always available or that a result fits you. Nothing here limits the rights you have by law as a consumer.</p>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may change slashkern and these terms. The date above shows the last change. If you keep using slashkern after a change, you accept it.</p>
      <h2>Law and contact</h2>
      <p>Italian law applies, and as a consumer you keep the protections of the country where you live. slashkern is run by Manuel Di Paolo (Italy). Contact: <a href="mailto:manuel@trykern.it">manuel@trykern.it</a>.</p>
